{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795275273,"nonce":"6NIj83h4UMLxcCF2TpPM3Fs7HOA=","title":"Six cn recorder goldens fail: three rendering regressions from ba3a0bcd and two goldens that predate fixes","message":"Six blinc_recorder tests failed on main against the macOS goldens recorded on 2026-11-10 and 2026-11-12. They had been passed over as stale. Bisected each against 2ca5f509 (all pass there) with a copy of the goldens through BLINC_SNAPSHOT_DIR.\n\ncn_input_snapshots: a_disabled_field_does_not_respond, an_error_keeps_its_border_while_hovered_and_focused, idle_hover_and_focus_follow_their_rules (cn_input_idle/error/disabled). First bad: ba3a0bcd. Since then a reactive translation is retained as a row translation with an empty motion binding, so a text input's text is collected as motion text and drawn as SDF primitives. Two faults on that path:\n- The SDF text branch clipped twice at a rect clip edge (calculate_clip_alpha, then a second smoothstep(0, 1, d)). A glyph touching its clip lost half of its first pixel column: column x=32 of \"Email\" went from coverage 45 to 35. Fixed by removing the second fade.\n- chain_moving/in_scroll_rows/under_scroll_row counted any row translation as moving, so the text was prepared unsnapped even when its content was painted into the static batch, where no row snaps it. Now only translations whose content is in the dynamic batch count.\n\ncn_pickers palette_updates_and_disabled_controls_preserve_the_value (cn_color_picker_disabled): first bad ba3a0bcd; the hex field's glyphs were unsnapped (the second fault above). Passes with the fix.\n\ncn_input_snapshots idle_hover_and_focus_follow_their_rules, next golden cn_input_focus (reached only now): still fails, 9 pixels, the same every run. The caret is drawn under the \"E\" of the placeholder: the golden's columns 32 and 33 both fit a caret at ~0.67 alpha over the text; now column 33 is the bare stem. The caret is a later sibling of the text in text_input/content.rs, so it belongs on top. Likely the same retention: the caret's translate and the text wrapper's scroll translate both get empty bindings, and the motion text pass draws after the batch that holds the caret canvas. Not proven: treating an empty binding whose content is in the static batch as ordinary content did not change it, and BLINC_MOTION_PROMOTION=1 takes a different path altogether.\n\ncn_pickers time_fields_wrap_and_preserve_unedited_parts (cn_time_picker_24_dark): first bad ba3a0bcd. All 372 differing pixels are on the picker's frame. `.cn-time-picker[data-focus-within]` sets border-color to the focus ring; the new frame shows it, the golden shows the idle border. The golden predates the headless runner applying state styles as the native runner does. Re-record.\n\ncn_select_snapshots a_long_combobox_list_stays_inside_its_popup (cn_combobox_long_list): first bad b09bb077 (re-apply class styles after VisualOnly and LayoutChanged updates, #71). The focused search field now shows `.cn-combobox-search:focus` border-color; the golden has none. Re-record.\n\nUnrelated failures seen in the same runs, all also failing on a clean a19f0b84: blinc_app rgba_order_primitive_cache_patchers_bail_before_mutation and foreground_layers_cache_patchers_request_full_paint_without_mutation (redraw_canvases returns true), blinc_layout stateful::tests::test_toggle_states and test_state_transition_with_enum (ignored), and the tbc BC4 canary (81183df).","files":null}]}